<title>POLAND: Polish KPW approves Universal ADR issue.</title>
<headline>Polish KPW approves Universal ADR issue.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) on Thursday approved an agreement between Polish trader Universal SA and the Bank of New York to list American Depositary Receipts (ADRs), the KPW head said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Jacek Socha said Universal was the fourth Polish firm to list shares as ADRs or Global Depositary Receipts (GDRs) after Mostostal Export, Stalexport and Bank Gdanski.</p>
<p>&quot;Universal is like Mostostal Export in that shares will be taken from those currently on the bourse, meaning that the number of shares listed on the domestic bourse will fall,&quot; Jacek Socha told a news conference.</p>
<p>Socha said that no more than 9.78 percent of the firm's shares approved for public trade could be issued as ADRs, which represents 10 percent of the firm's bourse shares.</p>
<p>Universal currently has 23,100,510 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- Steven Silber +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
